.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt PATINA-CLIPBOARD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-clipboard
.Nd the Patina desktop's clipboard menu
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the menu the bar's clipboard icon opens, at the bar's right end: what was copied lately,
newest first, with how long ago.
An image shows as a small picture.
.Pp
A click on an entry copies it again, so Ctrl+V pastes it, and closes the menu.
The cross at its right end deletes it, and Clear all deletes them all.
Pause stops new copies being kept, while those there stay.
Escape, a click elsewhere, or the icon again closes it; running it while one is open closes that
one.
.Pp
The history is kept by
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
not by this menu, so it goes on when the menu is closed, and copies outlive the app they came
from.
The menu reads it over
.Ql com.sectorflabs.Patina.Clipboard
on the session bus, and the bar shows the icon only while something serves it.
Under another desktop there is none.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATINA_SKIN
The skin to wear, as the bar sets it; otherwise the bar's config's.
.It Ev PATINA_HUD_EDGE
.Dq top
or
.Dq bottom :
which edge to open from.
.It Ev PATINA_OPEN_AT
Where the bar's button that opened it is, as
.Ql edge,x,y Ns Op ,far
in logical pixels: it opens just past it.
.El
